cata_final_en.tex:210:216: Warning: No match found for `('. Figure~\ref{fig:task1_radar} clarifies the strengths of CATA compared with the ViT+Qwen baseline: groups requiring morphological/location reasoning all improve substantially, including count 0.556$\rightarrow$0.700 (+25.9%), presence 0.577$\rightarrow$0.700 (+21.3%), instrument location 0.580$\rightarrow$0.698 (+20.3%), abnormality location 0.536$\rightarrow$0.650 (+21.3%), and polyp size 0.566$\rightarrow$0.678 (+19.8%). Even the color group, which depends more on appearance than topology, increases from 0.502 to 0.600 (+19.4%). This shows that the benefit of CATA does not come only from a stronger LLM, but from introducing TDA signals into both visual fusion and the decoder adapter, helping the model become more stable on questions requiring location, count, size, and morphological evidence; test adaptation only serves as an additional refinement compared with Epoch 5.  
